#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="src/**, lib/**, app/**, pages/**, server/**"

LANGUAGE_RUNTIME:
- TypeScript — strict mode on (fill in exact version, e.g. "5.4")
- Node.js 20 LTS (fill in exact version pin)
- pnpm — do not use npm or yarn

BUILD:
- pnpm build (adjust to actual build script)
- Type check: pnpm tsc --noEmit
- Lint: pnpm lint

STYLE_CONVENTIONS:
- strict TypeScript — no `any`, no untyped returns on exported functions
- Prettier for formatting — do not hand-format spacing or quotes
- ESLint rules are enforced — do not disable without a comment explaining why
- Named exports preferred over default exports
- No barrel files (index.ts re-export chains) unless explicitly in scope

FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS:
- No `as any` or `// @ts-ignore` without a comment justifying it
- No `console.log` in production paths — use the project logger
- No hardcoded secrets, API keys, or environment-specific strings in source
- No direct `process.exit()` in library code — throw or return errors

EXPLICITLY_NOT_TOUCHING:
- (fill in: generated files, lock files, vendored code, etc.)
